  "manual_code_review": [
    "The three source scheduling callbacks return directly. The environment functions allocate an 80-byte context, establish a mutex and process-lifetime run-loop thread, then stop/join/destroy/free it at finalization.",
    "Start obtains only the caller-supplied N-API path, event cursor and callback, copies a bounded 1024-byte path, builds a CF path array and FSEventStream with flags 0x15 and latency 0.1, then returns an external handle with cleanup callback.",
    "OS event paths/flags/IDs are copied into records and sent through the caller callback. Stop invalidates/releases the stream and callback; dispatch converts those three fields to JS values and frees event records. No file contents or credential stores are read by these functions.",
    "Initialization exposes five properties, 24 event flag constants, SinceNow=-1, NAPI version 4 and a registration jump to Init. Both architectures match these source flows.",
    "All 74 cold functions per architecture are assertion failures with one __assert_rtn call; linker stubs and helpers contain normal external binding sequences. All executable bytes are independently matched to the disassembly, with no unknown instructions or direct system calls.",
    "All native C strings match source identifiers, literal strings or exact CHECK/CONSTANT expansions. Loader bindings equal the 51 symbol imports; four system libraries only, no automatic initializer functions."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "This is an exact static source/code/loader-data review, not a reproducible build or a proof of memory safety.",
    "The source aborts on some invalid N-API inputs, does not check every allocation/thread result and may leak resources on exceptional shutdown. These reliability limits are not denied or turned into runtime guarantees.",
    "The normal watcher worker thread ends with its process; this review creates no daemon, login item or OS persistence.",
    "Registry metadata declares a node-gyp install hook. No hook, compiler, addon or crate is run, and this content review grants no execution/install/release approval.",
    "Unknown files, other fsevents versions and changed bytes remain blocking. No third-party binary, disassembly text, decoded source or Markdown is committed."
  ],
